@page "/release-notes"

@* The Release Notes (ADR-0190), a reference page: every version published to nuget.org up to the one the
   site was published for, newest first, one anchor each, read at build time from docs/releases/. Once a
   stable version exists, the site follows the latest one (ADR-0205), so a later prerelease's notes, or a
   patch's to an older line, are on its GitHub release until the next stable publish. A site not published
   from a tag also shows what is unreleased, from the Change Notes. Its sections are the versions, which
   the rail lists. *@
<DocsPage Title="Release notes"
          Lead="Every version published to nuget.org up to the one this site describes, newest first. A version's packages ship together, at one version, from one tag. Once a version without a suffix is out, this site describes the latest such version, and a version published after it that does not replace it, a prerelease or a patch to an older line, has its notes on its GitHub release until the next stable version brings them here.">
    <ReleaseNotesView />
</DocsPage>
